<GuideLayout
  title="What is Expert Edge"
  description="Expert Edge is a verification system for expert witnesses and consultants, cross-checked against public registries."
>
  <p>
    Expert Edge is a verification system for expert witnesses and consultants.
    Before a name goes on a witness list, into a deposition, or in front of a
    jury, Expert Edge cross-checks it against public registries — publications,
    retractions, funding, patents, litigation history, and licensure — and
    returns a single, defensible risk score.
  </p>
  <p>
    It covers five industries: <strong>MDL / Medical</strong>, <strong>Environmental Law</strong>, <strong>Financial</strong>, <strong>Engineering</strong>, and <strong>Scientific</strong>. Each
    industry has its own mix of signals — a medical expert's record leans on
    retractions and NIH funding, a financial expert's on disciplinary filings
    — but every record is scored against the same standard.
  </p>

  <h2>What it is not</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Not a background-check service for personal or criminal history.</li>
    <li>Not legal advice, and not a substitute for independent diligence on a specific engagement.</li>
    <li>Not a closed database — it's built to be pointed at your own expert list.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How it's built</h2>
  <p>
    A Python backend (<code>gatekeeper_backend_enhanced.py</code>) queries
    eight public sources and writes the results to <code>expert_data.json</code>.
    The site itself is a static Astro build — no server, no database, no CMS —
    that reads that file at runtime, so the directory can be refreshed
    independently of a redeploy. See <a href="/guide/data-sources/">Data Sources</a>
    for the full list, and <a href="/guide/scoring-system/">Scoring System</a>
    for how a record's risk level is calculated.
  </p>
</GuideLayout>
